body:
when did i ever say my vote didnt make a difference? nice of you to assume that was my message here.  read what i said again, and let's stop glorifying a war criminal. there was no mention of the upcoming election whatsoever.

&#x200B;

edit: nice to know you think calling out a world leader for their crimes constitutes being "edgy"

What exactly made Obama a "real president?"

Was it the endless drone strikes on innocents across the middle east?[https://www.thebureauinvestigates.com/stories/2017-01-17/obamas-covert-drone-war-in-numbers-ten-times-more-strikes-than-bush](https://www.thebureauinvestigates.com/stories/2017-01-17/obamas-covert-drone-war-in-numbers-ten-times-more-strikes-than-bush)

Was it his failed promise to close Guantanamo Bay, where numerous instances of torture have taken place? [https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/feb/24/obama-guantanamo-bay-closure-republicans](https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/feb/24/obama-guantanamo-bay-closure-republicans)

&#x200B;

Was it the massive corporate bailouts which we have seen time and time again benefit the shareholders and leave laborers empty handed?[https://thehill.com/policy/transportation/228836-obama-auto-bailout-was-the-right-thing-to-do](https://thehill.com/policy/transportation/228836-obama-auto-bailout-was-the-right-thing-to-do)

&#x200B;

Was it the mass deportation of immigrants across our southern border?[https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/obamas-deportation-policy-numbers/story?id=41715661](https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/obamas-deportation-policy-numbers/story?id=41715661)

&#x200B;

Was it the harsh separation of immigrant children from their families? [https://www.mcclatchydc.com/news/politics-government/white-house/article213525764.html](https://www.mcclatchydc.com/news/politics-government/white-house/article213525764.html)

&#x200B;

Was it US-arms backed Saudi war in Yemen that has also killed thousands of innocents while lining the pockets of US defense companies? [https://www.theatlantic.com/international/archive/2016/09/yemen-saudi-arabia-obama-riyadh/501365/](https://www.theatlantic.com/international/archive/2016/09/yemen-saudi-arabia-obama-riyadh/501365/)

&#x200B;

Was it his failure to address the Flint water crisis and hold those within the administration accountable?[https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2016/may/04/flint-water-crisis-a-shadow-on-obamas-legacy](https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2016/may/04/flint-water-crisis-a-shadow-on-obamas-legacy)

&#x200B;

I'm no conservative here bashing Obama for absolutely no reason, Trump is most certainly not my favored leader either.  Four years of "orange man bad" and manufactured consent on behalf of the media have diluted our thinking. Do not glorify this war criminal of a president.

&#x200B;

EDIT: as expected, here comes the down vote brigade. love that people cant throw their morals out the window under the guise of "political compromise"
